60,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Option C is completely out of the question. The daily setup time May mentioned and the recurring facilities costs for power would be a financial and operational disaster.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I agree with Victoria. Option C sounds very tiring because we would have to adjust our chairs and monitors every single day, and we might end up in the noisy spot by the printer.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,Option C is a total nightmare! I'm not spending my precious morning gaps fighting with cables and screens just to find out I'm sitting next to a loud printer. Absolutely not.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option C is a joke. As I mentioned, it's just a lottery for the early birds to snag the windows while the rest of us arrive to find the leftovers. It's not ""free,"" it's just unfair.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. Option C sounds too chaotic. If we're just picking random spots, we might end up far apart, and I'm worried we'll lose that feeling of being a team.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, since you are concerned about the disparity of the seats, Option B might seem appealing. However, rotating blocks would trigger those facilities charges repeatedly, which our budget simply cannot sustain. Option A is the most fiscally responsible.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I think Option A is the most peaceful. If we have our own desks, we can spend the time we need to make them fit our bodies perfectly and we won't have to worry about the noise changing every time we move.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Victoria, I'm with you on the budget, but more importantly, I'm with you on the stability! Option B sounds like a recipe for those ""fortnights of chaos"" I'm dreading. Why invite a mess when we can just settle in?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, you're very focused on the wallet, but Option A is just a polite way of saying ""the lucky few keep the windows forever."" If we go with A, we need to be explicit about who gets the wall.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Option A could work if we just talk about it. If we decide together where to sit, we can make sure we're close enough to help each other without the chaos of moving.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, I am not avoiding the issue of the ""wall."" I am simply stating that we must solve it through communication and agreement, not through a costly rotation system that drains our limited resources. Option A is the only sustainable choice.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I think Victoria is right. If we just talk and be kind to each other, we can decide the seats together. That way, everyone can have a cozy spot that feels just right for their body.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, honestly, just talk it out! I'd much rather have a slightly boring wall view than spend my life packing boxes and unplugging monitors. Let's just pick our spots and actually enjoy our mornings for once.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, ""talking it out"" is exactly what I'm suggesting, but let's not be naive. Someone always ends up with the worst spot. If we choose A, let's actually name the ""wall"" seats and decide who takes them now.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Shunichi is right that we should be honest about it. If we can just be open and decide together, maybe it won't feel so bad. I'll vote for Option A.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree with Daisuke. Option A provides the financial stability we need and the physical consistency Minato and May desire. Let us commit to a fair, transparent assignment process. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Minato"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'll vote for Option A too. It feels like the most peaceful way to make sure everyone is comfortable and happy in their own little space.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,I'm totally sold on A! No more cable chaos or packing boxes for me. Let's just settle in and keep our mornings stress-free. I vote for Option A!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Since everyone is so eager to avoid a little effort, I'll play along. Option A is the most rational choice, provided we stop pretending the seats are equal and actually assign the wall. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,pass,Daisuke,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
